§1. After baptism, the following are enrolled in another Church sui iuris:

1° a person who has obtained permission from the Apostolic See;

2° a spouse who, when entering marriage or during it, declares a transfer to the Church sui iuris of the other spouse; after the marriage is dissolved, that person may freely return to the Latin Church;

3° children of those mentioned in numbers 1 and 2, before completing fourteen years of age, and likewise, in a mixed marriage, children of the Catholic party who has lawfully transferred to another Church sui iuris; after reaching that age, they may return to the Latin Church.

§2. Receiving the sacraments according to the rite of another Church sui iuris, even over a long period, does not entail enrollment in that Church.

§3. Every transfer to another Church sui iuris takes effect when a declaration is made before the local ordinary of that Church, its proper pastor, or a priest delegated by either, and two witnesses, unless a rescript of the Apostolic See provides otherwise; it is to be recorded in the baptismal register.
